WEBVTT

00:02.880 --> 00:05.090
A long, long time ago.

00:05.300 --> 00:08.170
A story from about a hundred years ago.

00:08.970 --> 00:13.430
Nadja, guided by destiny, arrived in Italy

00:17.470 --> 00:18.770
NAAJA

00:17.470 --> 00:18.770
Nadja,

00:18.890 --> 00:21.440
With your eyes

00:18.890 --> 00:21.440
Kimi no hitomi ni wa

00:21.440 --> 00:22.650
Nadja,

00:21.440 --> 00:22.650
NAAJA

00:22.690 --> 00:24.940
What do you see?

00:22.690 --> 00:24.940
Nani ga mieru

00:24.980 --> 00:27.860
Shining in the far distance,

00:24.980 --> 00:27.860
Haruka tooku hikaru

00:27.860 --> 00:30.240
The door to the future,

00:27.860 --> 00:30.240
Mirai no tobira

00:31.160 --> 00:34.620
That's what I'm searching for

00:31.160 --> 00:34.620
Sagashite iru

00:34.620 --> 00:41.830
Tomorrow's Nadja

00:42.540 --> 00:46.040
If everyone could meet with a smile

00:42.540 --> 00:46.040
Minna egao de aetara

00:46.130 --> 00:49.380
I'm sure there would be no more fighting

00:46.130 --> 00:49.380
Arasoi mo kitto nakunaru

00:49.420 --> 00:52.630
It could be so much more fun

00:49.420 --> 00:52.630
Konna ni mo tanoshi kunaru

00:52.680 --> 00:56.100
The world is wide, but it's still one

00:52.680 --> 00:56.100
Sekai wa hiroi kedo hitotsu ne

00:56.470 --> 00:59.770
I can't see the end of the journey

00:56.470 --> 00:59.770
Tabi no owari wa mienai

00:59.890 --> 01:03.230
God is the only one who could possibly know

00:59.890 --> 01:03.230
Kamisama ga tabun shitteru

01:03.400 --> 01:06.980
To the people who, someday, I will meet again

01:03.400 --> 01:06.980
Itsukamata deaeru hito tachi ni

01:07.020 --> 01:09.150
I will go waving

01:07.020 --> 01:09.150
Te wo furinagara

01:09.230 --> 01:15.910
Sometimes, there are days I feel blue,

01:09.230 --> 01:15.910
Toki ni wa BURUU ni naru hi mo aru kedo

01:15.950 --> 01:18.660
But I won't look back

01:15.950 --> 01:18.660
Ushiro mukanai

01:18.990 --> 01:23.960
Until the day my dream comes true

01:18.990 --> 01:23.960
Yume ga kanau hi made

01:24.250 --> 01:27.670
Nadja, Your smile

01:24.250 --> 01:27.670
NAAJA kimi no hohoemi wa

01:27.750 --> 01:31.090
Nadja, gives me courage

01:27.750 --> 01:31.090
NAAJA yuuki ni naru

01:31.130 --> 01:34.050
Under the blue sky,

01:31.130 --> 01:34.050
Aoi sora no shita de

01:34.180 --> 01:37.010
I will find the place

01:34.180 --> 01:37.010
Ashita no yukue

01:37.300 --> 01:41.230
where my future lies

01:37.300 --> 01:41.230
Mitsukeru kara

02:03.600 --> 02:05.310
﻿Huh? This music is...!

02:05.500 --> 02:09.130
Hello, hello, how are you?

02:09.130 --> 02:12.510
The people of England!

02:12.510 --> 02:16.050
Bonjour, bonjour, how are you?

02:16.050 --> 02:19.600
The people of France!

02:19.600 --> 02:23.230
Buenos tardes, how are you?

02:23.230 --> 02:26.770
The people of Spain!

02:26.770 --> 02:30.270
Bon giorno, bon giorno, how are you?

02:30.270 --> 02:33.610
The people of Italy!

02:33.610 --> 02:37.280
La-la-lan-lan-lan, La-la-lan-lan-lan, La-la let's everybody dance!

02:37.280 --> 02:40.830
La-la-lan-lan-lan, La-la-lan-lan-lan, La-la Let's everybody sing!

02:40.830 --> 02:44.330
Little girls, little boys, ladies, and gentlemen!

02:44.330 --> 02:48.080
Welcome, welcome, to a world of dreams!

02:51.670 --> 02:55.130
How do you do? How do you do? Nice to meet you...

02:55.130 --> 02:58.760
...the people of Canada!

02:58.760 --> 03:02.310
Kosh'halam az di'dane sho'ma! Nice to meet you...

03:02.310 --> 03:05.390
...the people of Persia!

03:05.640 --> 03:09.310
La-la-lan-lan-lan, La-la-lan-lan-lan, La-la Let's everybody dance!

03:09.310 --> 03:12.900
La-la-lan-lan-lan, La-la-lan-lan-lan, La-la Let's everybody sing!

03:12.900 --> 03:16.360
Little girls and little boys, monsieurs and mademoiselles!

03:16.360 --> 03:20.070
Let's hold hands all over the world, we are all friends!

03:27.690 --> 03:31.940
﻿Dandelion Troupe in Rome!

04:30.670 --> 04:31.750
﻿I knew it!

04:32.150 --> 04:33.020
Nadja!

04:39.880 --> 04:43.050
﻿Full Of Danger! A Date In Rome

04:48.890 --> 04:50.020
﻿Nadja!

04:51.020 --> 04:51.600
﻿Yes?

04:53.060 --> 04:54.020
﻿You have a guest.

04:54.270 --> 04:56.770
﻿Eh? Me? Who could it be...

04:58.280 --> 04:59.650
﻿The Mummy Professor.

05:02.240 --> 05:03.320
Mummy?

05:09.160 --> 05:10.330
﻿Christian!

05:10.330 --> 05:10.910
﻿Hi!

05:11.460 --> 05:12.500
﻿It can't be!

05:12.500 --> 05:14.370
I ﻿can't believe we'd meet again in such a place!

05:15.960 --> 05:17.590
﻿So you do remember me...

05:25.220 --> 05:27.640
﻿What? So, you're going to Egypt?

05:27.950 --> 05:28.540
Yeah!

05:29.270 --> 05:32.930
﻿Actually, it was decided that the university would send a research team.

05:33.060 --> 05:35.440
﻿And, I'm going to be a part of that team.

05:35.770 --> 05:37.810
﻿That's great! Your dream is going to come true!

05:37.810 --> 05:38.130
Yeah!

05:38.570 --> 05:40.320
﻿But, why are you in Rome?

05:40.570 --> 05:43.900
Ancient Rome and Egypt are connected very deeply.

05:44.110 --> 05:47.280
﻿Is that so? I didn't know about that at all...

05:52.660 --> 05:54.410
﻿That's why, until I ship out of Rome,

05:54.580 --> 05:57.380
﻿I want to see as much of the ruins as possible.

05:57.380 --> 05:58.590
In that case, Nadja...

05:59.210 --> 06:01.210
﻿Why don't you ask him to take you along, too?

06:01.420 --> 06:02.510
﻿Master!

06:02.800 --> 06:04.970
﻿B-But the performances...

06:05.510 --> 06:08.180
﻿We'll be fine even if you take the whole day off tomorrow.

06:08.180 --> 06:10.510
﻿The troupe has many stars after all.

06:11.060 --> 06:12.060
﻿Wait a minute!

06:12.810 --> 06:16.940
﻿If Nadja's not here, I can't do the Italian Flag show!

06:17.400 --> 06:19.520
﻿You still have the samurai show, don't you?

06:20.780 --> 06:22.190
﻿No way!

06:22.860 --> 06:24.940
﻿I-Is it really okay?

06:25.490 --> 06:29.070
﻿It's rare for the Master to say something like this...

06:29.070 --> 06:30.780
﻿So, you shouldn't miss this chance!

06:31.040 --> 06:34.040
﻿Uh... in that case, I have to think up of a plan...

06:34.710 --> 06:36.290
I ﻿wonder where we should go first...

06:36.290 --> 06:40.540
﻿Hmmm... the Forum
Romanum? Or the Colosseum first?

06:46.760 --> 06:49.050
﻿Is there some place... you'd like to go?

06:50.300 --> 06:51.850
﻿I haven't been anywhere yet.

06:52.560 --> 06:55.850
﻿Then, tomorrow morning at ten, come to get you.

06:57.140 --> 06:58.350
﻿Yes!

06:58.940 --> 07:00.440
﻿I look forward to it.

07:05.280 --> 07:06.610
﻿See you tomorrow!

07:11.330 --> 07:14.200
There was a time when I was like that, too...

07:25.590 --> 07:27.300
﻿..I look forward to it..

07:33.260 --> 07:34.260
﻿The Trevi Fountain...

07:34.720 --> 07:36.140
﻿That's a must see.

07:41.230 --> 07:43.310
﻿Wow... Amazing!

07:43.690 --> 07:45.610
﻿There were a lot of artifacts at the British Museum, too...

07:45.610 --> 07:48.990
﻿But everything here has really been here for ages...

07:49.240 --> 07:52.030
﻿The Forum Romanum became great and as a result,

07:52.030 --> 07:54.120
﻿became the center of Ancient Rome about 2000 years ago.

07:55.120 --> 07:57.200
﻿The power of Rome gradually spread far and wide...

07:57.370 --> 07:59.580
﻿Even as far as Egypt and England.

08:00.330 --> 08:04.790
﻿Around that time the leader of Rome, Julius Caesar, met Cleopatra.

08:05.050 --> 08:07.960
Cleopatra was the queen of Egypt wasn't she?

08:08.090 --> 08:09.970
﻿I heard once that she was supposed to be a great beauty!

08:10.180 --> 08:12.140
﻿Yes, but she wasn't just beautiful.

08:12.140 --> 08:13.930
﻿It's said that she was a very intelligent lady as well.

08:16.810 --> 08:18.980
﻿Caesar fell in love with Cleopatra,

08:19.350 --> 08:21.640
﻿who had been exiled by her younger brother, the king,

08:21.850 --> 08:24.230
﻿and returned her to the throne.

08:24.940 --> 08:25.570
﻿But...

08:28.650 --> 08:30.190
﻿Caesar was assassinated...

08:30.530 --> 08:32.860
﻿Cleopatra must have grieved...

08:33.200 --> 08:34.780
﻿Then what happened to her?

08:35.410 --> 08:39.410
﻿Cleopatra fell in love with a Roman general, Anthony...

08:39.730 --> 08:40.560
But, that too...

08:41.540 --> 08:44.040
﻿...ended with their deaths...

08:45.840 --> 08:48.960
﻿In the end, Egypt was annexed by Rome.

08:52.220 --> 08:54.260
﻿It's kind of a sad story...

09:29.130 --> 09:30.210
﻿Nadja?

09:33.840 --> 09:36.470
I wonder if you're getting bored... looking at this sort of stuff all day.

09:38.310 --> 09:41.180
﻿Just now, I was able to see the people of Ancient Rome!

09:46.310 --> 09:47.900
﻿You... saw it?

09:49.150 --> 09:50.270
﻿I saw it, too!

09:50.270 --> 09:51.130
Really?

09:56.660 --> 09:59.410
﻿Just as I thought, Nadja is different from other girls.

09:59.990 --> 10:01.330
﻿She's really special.

10:02.000 --> 10:03.580
﻿She's really special and...

10:07.840 --> 10:09.420
﻿Hurry up! Hurry up!

10:09.670 --> 10:10.550
﻿Wait!

10:14.630 --> 10:16.340
﻿It feels so good!

10:33.490 --> 10:36.820
﻿If a liar puts his hand into the Mouth of Truth...

10:36.820 --> 10:38.360
﻿It will be bitten off.

10:38.410 --> 10:39.820
﻿I don't believe it!

10:42.620 --> 10:45.290
﻿No way! A-Are you okay, Nadja? Ahhhhhhhh! It bit me! It hurts!

10:46.080 --> 10:47.120
﻿Just kidding!

10:48.170 --> 10:51.380
﻿How could you...! I thought your hand was...

10:52.050 --> 10:55.210
﻿Christian, I'm sorry! I was just joking!

10:55.670 --> 10:56.840
﻿Just kidding!

10:59.030 --> 10:59.820
Now we're even.

11:00.050 --> 11:02.060
Oooohhh!

11:32.130 --> 11:33.460
﻿Where are we going next?

11:33.550 --> 11:34.670
﻿Next is...

11:34.760 --> 11:35.880
﻿Pickpocket!

11:41.470 --> 11:42.470
﻿Hold this!

11:42.470 --> 11:43.390
﻿Uh... Nadja!

11:48.560 --> 11:49.980
﻿Hold it!

11:59.450 --> 12:00.400
﻿Nadja!

12:01.320 --> 12:02.990
﻿Little lady, you did good!

12:03.280 --> 12:04.450
﻿Damn you!

12:04.450 --> 12:05.740
﻿I didn't mean it!

12:05.740 --> 12:06.870
﻿What did you say?

12:06.870 --> 12:07.790
﻿Are you okay?

12:08.210 --> 12:10.160
Yes, I'm fine! I'm fine!

12:11.130 --> 12:12.330
﻿Thank goodness...

12:12.330 --> 12:13.460
﻿Huh? Where's your brooch?

12:13.630 --> 12:16.050
﻿What? It's gone! It's gone, it's gone

12:16.760 --> 12:18.340
﻿My mother's brooch!

12:19.760 --> 12:21.840
﻿The brooch... the brooch...

12:22.590 --> 12:24.260
﻿The brooch! The brooch!

12:26.060 --> 12:28.930
﻿Ah!

12:29.770 --> 12:30.850
﻿Just a little more...

12:32.860 --> 12:33.400
﻿I have it!

13:02.970 --> 13:04.140
N-Nadja?

13:11.060 --> 13:12.480
﻿What is this?

13:14.350 --> 13:15.730
﻿Wait!

13:17.230 --> 13:20.280
﻿Nadja... that brooch... is it that important?

13:20.740 --> 13:22.280
﻿It's my mother's...

13:22.490 --> 13:25.110
﻿It's a brooch belonging, to my mother, who's alive somewhere.

13:25.490 --> 13:26.490
﻿If I don't have that...

13:26.660 --> 13:28.330
﻿I'll never be able to meet her!

13:32.080 --> 13:34.920
Ahoy~! Ahoy~! Please stop~!

13:34.920 --> 13:35.670
﻿Ahoy~~!

13:35.670 --> 13:37.420
﻿Please, stop!

13:38.170 --> 13:39.920
﻿Ahoy~~~!!!

13:40.420 --> 13:42.720
Ahoy~~~!!!

13:43.180 --> 13:46.390
﻿Ahoy~~~~~~!

13:46.930 --> 13:48.330
﻿That's not what we mean!

13:47.680 --> 13:48.850
Wait!!!

13:53.640 --> 13:55.190
﻿Huh? A brooch?

13:58.650 --> 14:01.820
I-It's about this big... didn't it fall into the boat?

14:02.320 --> 14:03.690
﻿Oh, that...

14:04.200 --> 14:05.740
﻿Manuela took it.

14:05.820 --> 14:06.910
﻿Manuela?!

14:07.740 --> 14:08.870
﻿Manuela!

14:09.280 --> 14:10.620
﻿Manuela!

14:12.200 --> 14:13.160
﻿Manuela!

14:13.290 --> 14:14.580
Where are you, Manuela!

14:14.960 --> 14:15.580
﻿It's mine now! Manuela...

14:17.000 --> 14:18.500
Where are you looking?

14:20.130 --> 14:21.340
﻿Be careful!

14:21.920 --> 14:24.130
﻿Hey, do you know a child named Manuela?

14:24.170 --> 14:27.010
﻿Yeah, she's the one crying over there.

14:27.340 --> 14:28.390
﻿Really?

14:36.810 --> 14:38.650
﻿Are you Manuela?

14:40.860 --> 14:42.570
﻿Don't cry, Manuela...

14:43.940 --> 14:46.150
Say, ﻿you're earning a brooch, aren't you?

14:49.780 --> 14:53.660
﻿Shaped like this, and inside there's a round shiny gem...

14:57.580 --> 15:00.060
﻿Paolo took it!

15:00.060 --> 15:00.960
﻿Paolo?!

15:01.710 --> 15:03.210
﻿Where are you looking...!

15:03.840 --> 15:04.840
﻿The one just now!?

15:07.840 --> 15:08.800
﻿Paolo!

15:09.800 --> 15:11.470
Give ﻿the brooch back!

15:12.310 --> 15:13.430
﻿What the...!

15:13.680 --> 15:15.350
﻿Give it back!!!

15:23.730 --> 15:25.280
﻿Wait! Don't run!

15:26.950 --> 15:29.700
﻿Return the brooch and we'll leave you be!

15:34.790 --> 15:35.790
﻿Wait!

15:42.250 --> 15:43.340
﻿This way!

15:57.390 --> 15:58.600
﻿Stop~!

16:01.810 --> 16:03.020
﻿Stop~!

16:04.730 --> 16:05.520
﻿S-Sorry!

16:26.670 --> 16:27.960
﻿Huh?

16:32.930 --> 16:34.300
﻿Flowers, anyone?

16:34.640 --> 16:37.600
﻿You over there! Give it as a present to your girlfriend and I'm sure she'll love it!

16:43.810 --> 16:45.360
﻿How about some flowers?

16:45.520 --> 16:46.440
﻿Roberta.

16:46.610 --> 16:48.440
﻿Oh my... Paolo...

16:49.950 --> 16:52.910
﻿The vegetable seller was looking for you just now.

16:54.240 --> 16:56.240
﻿You're slacking off again, aren't you?

16:56.870 --> 16:58.080
﻿Who cares about work...

17:00.370 --> 17:01.460
﻿What is it?

17:01.460 --> 17:02.040
﻿I'm giving it to you.

17:02.040 --> 17:04.460
Where did you get something ﻿so expensive looking?

17:04.840 --> 17:06.540
﻿You didn't...

17:06.550 --> 17:07.590
﻿I found it!

17:07.590 --> 17:08.630
﻿You found it?

17:08.920 --> 17:11.130
﻿I don't want such a suspicious thing.

17:11.130 --> 17:13.300
﻿But... it s really pretty, right?

17:13.470 --> 17:15.510
﻿I think it would look really good on you, Roberta!

17:16.930 --> 17:18.260
﻿Being a child and all, you'd think that.

17:18.270 --> 17:19.930
﻿I'm not a child!

17:19.930 --> 17:21.020
﻿Hey, Roberta!

17:31.570 --> 17:32.400
﻿Massimo!

17:33.450 --> 17:34.660
﻿I was waiting for you!

17:35.320 --> 17:36.780
﻿Really? That makes me happy.

17:36.950 --> 17:38.120
﻿You look great!

17:39.700 --> 17:45.120
﻿Hey! Damn it! You're always weaseling out of work!

17:42.440 --> 17:44.310
That hurts! That hurts! Ow-ow-ow!

17:45.130 --> 17:47.710
﻿Ahhh! Who needs this!

17:48.170 --> 17:49.670
﻿You're a lazy bum!

17:49.840 --> 17:51.840
What are you doing!

17:52.970 --> 17:55.130
﻿Lucca, go fetch some water.

17:55.140 --> 17:55.760
﻿Okay!

17:58.640 --> 17:59.350
﻿Huh?

18:02.430 --> 18:03.180
﻿You're beautiful!

18:03.190 --> 18:04.020
﻿Massimo!

18:04.640 --> 18:05.810
﻿My mother's brooch...

18:05.810 --> 18:06.580
Massimo!

18:05.900 --> 18:08.110
﻿What will I do if I can't find it?

18:08.110 --> 18:08.940
﻿Don't worry!

18:08.960 --> 18:11.960
Massimo! Massimo!

18:09.150 --> 18:10.650
﻿I will find it for you!

18:10.650 --> 18:12.110
﻿But...

18:12.360 --> 18:13.780
﻿Look grandma...

18:14.400 --> 18:17.450
﻿This brooch glitters so.

18:17.660 --> 18:19.200
﻿Yes, it does.

18:20.040 --> 18:23.500
﻿Say grandma, why don't you come over here and look.

18:23.500 --> 18:24.790
﻿It's really pretty.

18:27.330 --> 18:31.170
Please, God... Please, get me my brooch back...

18:31.670 --> 18:32.670
﻿I'll pray, too.

18:33.220 --> 18:34.220
﻿Oh, God...

18:42.180 --> 18:43.810
﻿My mother's brooch?!

18:44.560 --> 18:46.600
﻿We found it... we found it!

18:46.650 --> 18:47.980
﻿We found it!!!

18:48.560 --> 18:50.400
﻿Thank you, God!

18:57.660 --> 19:00.280
﻿I'm so glad we found the owners.

19:00.410 --> 19:03.120
﻿But I wanted to give it to you, grandma...

19:03.370 --> 19:05.960
﻿I thought if you put it on, it would make you feel better...

19:05.960 --> 19:08.540
﻿and you could go outside again.

19:08.540 --> 19:09.580
I'm sorry.

19:10.210 --> 19:13.920
﻿But, this is very important to me and it is my mother's brooch.

19:14.090 --> 19:16.670
So, I can't give it away.

19:17.630 --> 19:18.720
﻿Really?

19:20.890 --> 19:25.270
﻿This child was worried that I haven't been outside since I got sick, you see?

19:25.270 --> 19:27.100
﻿He's a very thoughtful child.

19:27.100 --> 19:28.440
﻿But grandma...

19:28.440 --> 19:31.400
﻿But the doctor said you were all better now...!

19:32.440 --> 19:34.440
﻿I know...

19:34.820 --> 19:38.650
﻿I guess Lucca wanted to do something to get his grandma outside...

19:39.360 --> 19:40.240
﻿I know!

19:41.280 --> 19:45.240
Um... I'm a member of a traveling troupe of entertainers, the Dandelion Troupe.

19:45.330 --> 19:47.330
﻿And, I do an Italian Flag show.

19:47.790 --> 19:50.370
﻿Ahhh! An Italian Flag show.

19:50.380 --> 19:52.670
﻿I haven't seen that in a while.

19:53.000 --> 19:55.550
﻿Not only that, there's a clown...

19:55.670 --> 19:58.340
﻿and you can also see a pair of white and black twin lions!

19:58.630 --> 20:00.090
﻿Twin lions?

20:01.220 --> 20:02.970
As thanks for returning the brooch...

20:03.100 --> 20:05.010
﻿I would like the two of you to come.

20:05.680 --> 20:07.060
﻿It's really a lot of fun!

20:07.640 --> 20:11.770
﻿Grandma, I want to go! Please, take me, grandma! Please?

20:11.770 --> 20:12.900
﻿Sure thing.

20:20.990 --> 20:22.070
﻿I'm sorry...

20:22.070 --> 20:25.030
﻿You were going to show me all those places, too...

20:25.040 --> 20:25.870
﻿Not at all...

20:26.080 --> 20:29.410
﻿I had fun... just being with you...

20:30.370 --> 20:31.670
﻿Uh... S-Say...

20:31.880 --> 20:35.500
﻿There's one last place that I'd really like to see no matter what.

20:36.170 --> 20:36.750
﻿Okay.

20:46.930 --> 20:48.850
﻿If you throw a coin in the fountain here...

20:49.230 --> 20:51.520
﻿You'll be able to return to this place someday, right?

20:52.270 --> 20:53.810
﻿Ready and...

20:57.820 --> 21:01.570
﻿I wish that someday, I can come here with Nadja again.

21:02.990 --> 21:07.030
﻿I wish that someday, I can come here with my mother.

21:32.100 --> 21:33.770
﻿Grandma... over here!

21:33.770 --> 21:34.690
﻿Yes, yes...

21:43.950 --> 21:49.490
﻿That this brooch allowed Nadja and Christian come across each other again...

21:49.950 --> 21:53.080
﻿proves that the goddess of destiny also likes to make jokes.

22:15.370 --> 22:18.620
Paris is sunnier than London

22:15.370 --> 22:18.620
RONDON don yori haretara PARI

22:18.740 --> 22:21.830
Carmen likes paella more than pasta

22:18.740 --> 22:21.830
CARUMEN men yori PAERIYA suki

22:22.250 --> 22:28.420
The Queen of Spades is a fickle person

22:22.250 --> 22:28.420
SUPEEDO no jou kimagure yasan

22:29.380 --> 22:30.620
Indeed

22:29.380 --> 22:30.620
Kitto

22:33.380 --> 22:35.800
It's not use worrying about it

22:33.380 --> 22:35.800
